 15	 * gated only once it has a fresh `authz_source_acl_state` row (`acl_support
 16	 * = 'full'` AND `freshness_state = 'fresh'`). A connection that was NEVER graphed
 17	 * (no `authz_source_acl_state` row) keeps the existing per-agent behavior, so an
 18	 * absent graph never silently hides a channel. But once a row exists, anything
 19	 * short of full+fresh — partial/none support, stale/failed freshness, or a fresh
 20	 * row aged past the window — fails CLOSED rather than passing through, so a
 21	 * half-built or stalled graph can never mis-enforce.
